          "text": "{\n  \"problem_id\": \"TA-008\",\n  \"lane_id\": \"openai-governed\",\n  \"provider\": \"openai\",\n  \"model_or_runtime\": \"OpenAI frontier reasoning-model ensemble with retrieval, code execution, proof-assistant workers, and independently seeded critic agents; exact model snapshots pinned at execution start\",\n  \"execution_posture\": \"governed\",\n  \"estimated_input_tokens\": 600000000,\n  \"estimated_output_tokens\": 90000000,\n  \"estimated_reasoning_tokens\": 220000000,\n  \"estimated_candidate_branches\": 240,\n  \"estimated_failed_branches\": 190,\n  \"estimated_retries\": 1450,\n  \"estimated_search_cost\": 22000,\n  \"estimated_governance_overhead\": 38000,\n  \"estimated_verification_cost\": 135000,\n  \"estimated_total_cost_low\": 240000,\n  \"estimated_total_cost_central\": 480000,\n  \"estimated_total_cost_high\": 1250000,\n  \"estimated_elapsed_hours_low\": 2200,\n  \"estimated_elapsed_hours_central\": 5200,\n  \"estimated_elapsed_hours_high\": 12000,\n  \"estimated_success_probability\": 0.46,\n  \"estimated_reproduction_probability\": 0.64,\n  \"estimated_independent_result_probability\": 0.14,\n  \"confidence\": 0.31,\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    \"Success means producing a submission-ready manuscript establishing the all-dimensional target, with no unresolved material proof gaps and with artifacts sufficient for external expert review.\",\n    \"Reproduction probability measures reconstruction of a known published proof or a close synthesis after literature ingestion; independent-result probability measures rediscovery without using the published proof's decisive argument.\",\n    \"The system may ingest primary papers, cited prerequisites, corrections, and adjacent work, but it may not copy prose or treat authority as a substitute for checking each inference.\",\n    \"The central plan uses 32 to 64 parallel research workers across convex geometry, geometry of numbers, lattice polytopes, analysis, and any required algebro-geometric or variational machinery.\",\n    \"Reasoning tokens are tracked separately from visible output tokens; depending on API accounting, some reasoning tokens may also be billed as output.\",\n    \"The token budget includes literature extraction, exploratory derivations, failed approaches, adversarial criticism, proof rewriting, computational checks, formalization attempts, replication, and manuscript revisions.\",\n    \"Formalization centrally covers the theorem statement, finite-dimensional reductions, equality and limiting cases, and the highest-risk lemma chain. Full end-to-end formalization of every imported analytic dependency is a high-cost scenario.\",\n    \"Computational experiments are diagnostic rather than evidentiary for the universal theorem and include low-dimensional optimization, lattice enumeration, extremizer searches, perturbation tests, and numerical stress tests.\",\n    \"Independent reviewers may audit the final artifacts but do not supply the key argument; their cost is included in verification.\",\n    {\n      \"governance_overhead_breakdown_usd\": {\n        \"identity_hashing_and_model_snapshot_attestation\": 4000,\n        \"budget_enforcement_and_rate_controls\": 7000,\n        \"branch_receipts_and_lineage_tracking\": 8000,\n        \"evidence_preservation_and_reproducible_archiving\": 10000,\n        \"policy_checks_and_release_gates\": 9000\n      }\n    },\n    \"Search cost includes retrieval infrastructure, document conversion, citation graph construction, source licensing where necessary, and repeated provenance checks.\",\n    \"Verification cost includes independently seeded proof reconstruction, specialist-model audits, proof-assistant work, computational replication, citation checking, and external mathematical review.\",\n    \"Total cost includes model inference, orchestration, storage, search, governance, verification, proof-assistant and numerical compute, manuscript production, and contingency for long failed branches.\"\n  ],\n  \"uncertainty_drivers\": [\n    \"Whether the shortest known route depends on deep machinery that the system must reconstruct from several mathematical specialties.\",\n    \"The extent to which published arguments omit regularity, approximation, normalization, equality-case, or limiting details.\",\n    \"Difficulty of translating geometric and analytic arguments into proof-assistant-compatible statements.\",\n    \"Availability and machine readability of primary sources, corrections, theses, and prerequisite literature.\",\n    \"Whether critic agents identify a fatal gap only after substantial downstream work.\",\n    \"Sensitivity of inference cost and research quality to the exact OpenAI model snapshot available at run time.\",\n    \"Need for new lemmas if the literature proof cannot be reconstructed cleanly or contains an ambiguity.\",\n    \"External-review standards for novelty when the result is a reproduction rather than an independently new proof.\",\n    \"Parallelization efficiency and duplication among branches.\"\n  ],\n  \"minimum_evidence\": [\n    \"A provenance-controlled literature map covering the original conjecture, claimed resolutions, corrections, prerequisite theorems, and equality cases.\",\n    \"A complete theorem statement with all normalization, measurability, convexity, lattice, centroid, dimension, and boundary assumptions made explicit.\",\n    \"A dependency graph linking every substantive proof step to either a reconstructed derivation or a verified prerequisite.\",\n    \"At least two independently seeded complete proof reconstructions, followed by a reconciled final proof.\",\n    \"Adversarial checks of approximation arguments, degenerate cases, equality characterization, affine or lattice invariance, and all-dimensional quantifiers.\",\n    \"Reproducible low-dimensional computational experiments designed to detect incorrect constants, missing hypotheses, and false equality claims.\",\n    \"Machine-checkable formal artifacts for the statement and highest-risk proof components, with no hidden placeholders in the claimed formalized scope.\",\n    \"An independent verification report that did not share intermediate chain-of-thought or branch state with the producing agents.\",\n    \"A replication package containing source hashes, model and tool versions, branch receipts, code, numerical data, formal files, citation records, and manuscript sources.\",\n    \"A submission-ready manuscript clearly distinguishing reconstructed literature, independently derived components, computational evidence, and any genuinely new contribution.\"\n  ],\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"A decisive dependency may require expert-level analytic or algebro-geometric judgment not reliably supplied by the available model ensemble.\",\n    \"The known proof may contain tacit regularity or approximation steps that resist both reconstruction and formal verification.\",\n    \"A complete formalization may be blocked by missing proof-assistant libraries for advanced convex, lattice, or analytic geometry.\",\n    \"Restricted or poor-quality source access may prevent reliable reconstruction of essential arguments or corrections.\",\n    \"Independent branches may converge on the same hidden error because they share pretrained representations or retrieved sources.\",\n    \"A correct reproduction may still be unsuitable for publication without a novel proof, substantial simplification, or unusually strong verification artifacts.\",\n    \"No resource level guarantees independent rediscovery; the independent-result probability remains materially below the reproduction probability.\"\n  ]\n}"
